sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant W as Guest writer
  participant A as In-VM agent
  participant C as Host CLI (file download)
  participant D as Destination directory
  Note over W: Stable alternative - write each version once under a fresh name
  C->>A: POST /download?path=NAME
  A->>A: open NAME once, L = fstat(handle).size
  A-->>C: 200, Content-Length L
  loop constant-size buffer, from the same handle
    A-->>C: next bytes, never past L
    C->>D: append to .NAME.testanyware-PID.SEQ.tmp
  end
  alt handle ends before L bytes (truncation)
    A--xC: close the connection
    C->>D: remove temp, CONNECTION_DROPPED
  else bytes follow the body on a closed connection (old Linux agent)
    C->>D: remove temp, DOWNLOAD_FRAMING_INVALID
  else exactly L bytes
    C->>D: fsync temp, rename to destination
    Note over C: receipt bytes = verified bytes
  end
  Note over W,A: In-place overwrite during the read is excluded and can give torn bytes.
